WEBVTT

1
00:00:14.997 --> 00:00:20.702
Mary stood with her back against the door, looking around with excitement, wonder, and delight.

2
00:00:21.823 --> 00:00:23.984
She was standing inside the secret garden!

3
00:00:25.065 --> 00:00:27.847
It was the sweetest, most mysterious-looking place.

4
00:00:29.028 --> 00:00:33.192
The high walls were covered with the bare stems of roses that had grown together thickly.

5
00:00:34.592 --> 00:00:39.115
The ground was covered with brown grass that had clumps of rosebushes growing out of it.

6
00:00:40.375 --> 00:00:44.978
Some of the roses had run up the trees and swung down now from the branches in long

7
00:00:45.058 --> 00:00:50.601
tendrils. Mary recognized these plants because she'd seen roses growing in India.

8
00:00:51.802 --> 00:00:54.343
But she didn't know if they were dead or alive.

9
00:00:54.363 --> 00:00:59.126
"I hope the garden isn't dead," she said in a whisper.

10
00:00:59.146 --> 00:01:03.288
"I am the first person to enter this place in ten years."

11
00:01:04.540 --> 00:01:10.842
As Mary walked along, quietly examining the roses, the robin hopped about or flew after her from one

12
00:01:10.882 --> 00:01:11.842
bush to another.

13
00:01:13.023 --> 00:01:15.563
Mary stopped where there had once been a flower bed.

14
00:01:17.084 --> 00:01:21.825
She spotted some pale green points sticking out of the black earth and knelt down to look at

15
00:01:21.885 --> 00:01:25.987
them. "They are tiny growing things," she whispered.

16
00:01:26.007 --> 00:01:30.048
"Perhaps there are more coming up in other places."

17
00:01:32.532 --> 00:01:35.494
Mary looked in the old border beds and among the grass.

18
00:01:36.735 --> 00:01:39.817
She grew more excited as she found more pale green points.

19
00:01:39.837 --> 00:01:42.779
"It isn't quite a dead garden!"

20
00:01:43.340 --> 00:01:44.000
she cried out.

21
00:01:44.020 --> 00:01:48.463
"Even if the roses are dead, there are other things alive."

22
00:01:49.624 --> 00:01:51.585
Mary didn't know anything about gardening.

23
00:01:52.946 --> 00:01:57.249
But the grass seemed too thick in some places where the green points were trying to push their

24
00:01:57.289 --> 00:01:57.850
way through.

25
00:01:58.970 --> 00:02:01.092
She searched until she found a sharp stick.

26
00:02:02.216 --> 00:02:07.140
Then she dug out the grass and old weeds until she had cleared some space around the plants.

27
00:02:07.160 --> 00:02:10.123
"Now they look as if they could breathe!"

28
00:02:11.965 --> 00:02:15.007
Mary went from place to place and dug and weeded.

29
00:02:16.168 --> 00:02:19.711
The exercise made her so warm that she threw off her hat and coat.

30
00:02:20.912 --> 00:02:24.555
She worked happily in the garden until it was time to go inside for lunch.

31
00:02:25.917 --> 00:02:29.540
Martha was delighted when she saw Mary's bright eyes and rosy cheeks.

32
00:02:31.036 --> 00:02:34.958
She was even happier when Mary ate two helpings of meat and rice pudding.

33
00:02:36.398 --> 00:02:39.960
"Mother will be pleased when I tell her what skipping rope has done for you!"

34
00:02:41.040 --> 00:02:42.301
Mary did not reply.

35
00:02:42.861 --> 00:02:46.482
She was thinking about the strange white roots she had come across while digging.

36
00:02:48.043 --> 00:02:49.844
Perhaps Martha would know what they were.

37
00:02:49.864 --> 00:02:53.786
"I saw something that looked like an onion in the garden today."

38
00:02:54.906 --> 00:02:57.387
She was careful not to say the secret garden.

39
00:02:57.407 --> 00:02:59.468
"Those are bulbs.

40
00:02:59.932 --> 00:03:05.314
Lots of spring flowers grow from them: snowdrops, crocuses, daffodils, lilies.

41
00:03:05.855 --> 00:03:08.936
Dickon's got a whole lot of them planted in our bit of a garden."

42
00:03:10.476 --> 00:03:14.558
Mary had finished eating, so she went to sit in front of the fire.

43
00:03:15.819 --> 00:03:17.559
"I wish I had a little shovel."

44
00:03:18.720 --> 00:03:19.580
Martha laughed.

45
00:03:19.600 --> 00:03:21.601
"Are you going to start digging?"

46
00:03:22.822 --> 00:03:24.442
Mary knew she had to be careful.

47
00:03:25.643 --> 00:03:26.083
If Mr.

48
00:03:26.143 --> 00:03:30.225
Craven found out that someone had opened the door, he would be very angry.

49
00:03:31.686 --> 00:03:34.647
He might even get a new key and lock up the garden forever.

50
00:03:35.808 --> 00:03:37.108
She really could not bear that.

51
00:03:37.128 --> 00:03:42.191
"This is such a big, lonely place," she said slowly.

52
00:03:42.211 --> 00:03:47.914
"There is no one to talk to except you and Ben, and you both have work to do.

53
00:03:49.115 --> 00:03:53.077
If I had a shovel, I might ask him for some seeds and make a little garden."

54
00:03:54.558 --> 00:03:55.798
Martha's face lit up.

55
00:03:55.818 --> 00:03:58.240
"That's just what Mother suggested.

56
00:03:58.908 --> 00:04:02.210
At Thwaite village, there's a shop where they sell little garden sets.

57
00:04:02.850 --> 00:04:04.751
And they sell packages of flower seeds.

58
00:04:05.891 --> 00:04:09.493
We could write a letter to Dickon and ask him to buy them for you.

59
00:04:10.693 --> 00:04:14.615
He walks to Thwaite almost every day, and he knows all about growing things."

60
00:04:16.095 --> 00:04:19.297
"Oh, you are so nice," Mary exclaimed.

61
00:04:21.078 --> 00:04:23.099
Martha ran to fetch a pen and paper.

62
00:04:24.259 --> 00:04:24.939
But when Mrs.

63
00:04:24.999 --> 00:04:29.245
Medlock spotted Martha, she gave the maid one job and then another to do.

64
00:04:30.406 --> 00:04:33.187
So it was quite a while before Martha returned to Mary.

65
00:04:34.347 --> 00:04:37.809
When they finished writing the letter to Dickon, Mary had a question.

66
00:04:37.829 --> 00:04:41.210
"Does the kitchen maid have a toothache again today?"

67
00:04:42.311 --> 00:04:43.371
Martha looked startled.

68
00:04:43.911 --> 00:04:45.052
"What makes you ask that?"

69
00:04:45.072 --> 00:04:50.574
"Because while I was waiting for you to come back, I opened the door and walked down the

70
00:04:50.614 --> 00:04:53.595
corridor. And I heard that crying again."

71
00:04:53.615 --> 00:04:59.455
"Oh, you mustn't walk around listening like that," Martha said nervously.

72
00:04:59.475 --> 00:05:01.437
"Mr. Craven would be angry."

73
00:05:01.457 --> 00:05:05.500
"I wasn't trying to listen," Mary insisted.

74
00:05:05.520 --> 00:05:07.442
"I was just waiting for you.

75
00:05:07.902 --> 00:05:09.784
That's three times I've heard crying."

76
00:05:09.804 --> 00:05:12.106
"There's Mrs.

77
00:05:12.146 --> 00:05:12.986
Medlock's bell!"

78
00:05:13.527 --> 00:05:16.349
said Martha, and she practically ran from the room.

79
00:05:16.369 --> 00:05:20.452
"This is the strangest house," said Mary.

80
00:05:21.573 --> 00:05:24.776
But before she could think much more about it, she fell asleep.

81
00:05:25.965 --> 00:05:28.298
Fresh air and digging had made her drowsy.
